window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-ryuuen-kakeru"]=[{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 4  named before he is seen the volume names him for the first time in ichinose s warning   someone named ryuuen kun masterminded that one    the earlier class b class c dispute  and the sudou setup behind this case  as ichinose describes him   he doesn t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests  he s a formidable opponent  she adds that he  hasn t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet  which is why ayanokoji does not know the name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.4: named before he is seen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.241<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The volume names him for the first time in Ichinose’s warning: &quot;Someone named Ryuuen-kun masterminded that one.&quot; — the earlier Class B–Class C dispute, and the Sudou setup behind this case.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> As Ichinose describes him: &quot;He doesn’t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests. He’s a formidable opponent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She adds that he &quot;hasn’t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet,&quot; which is why Ayanokōji does not know the name.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.6: the boy in the corridor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 6  the boy in the corridor he stops in front of ayanokoji and horikita in the corridor   black hair worn long  about ayanokoji s height  a wide grin the page calls ominous  never fully turning to face them  the scene does not name him   setting up a camera  you really did something funny  huh   next time  i ll be your opponent  i look forward to it  he walks on without answering horikita s  and you are  ayanokoji s closing inventory names the encounter   we d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as ryuuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.6: the boy in the corridor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.254–255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He stops in front of Ayanokōji and Horikita in the corridor — black hair worn long, about Ayanokōji’s height, a wide grin the page calls ominous, never fully turning to face them. The scene does not name him.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Setting up a camera? You really did something funny, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Next time, I’ll be your opponent. I look forward to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He walks on without answering Horikita’s &quot;And you are?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ayanokōji’s closing inventory names the encounter: &quot;We’d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as Ryuuen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.4: named before he is seen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  3 2  the beach at zero holds court on the class c beach in swimwear   tanned  laid back in his chair  flashing white teeth   just as you see  we re enjoying our summer vacation   hmm  well  i didn t make a precise calculation  pours his remaining water on the sand  almost in provocation  while ishizaki fetches another bottle   class d  the lowest of all  has to put up with starvation  heat  and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points  it makes me laugh   i said to bring me cold water  this water s warm   ryuuen s pupils were just like those of a snake    the returned bottle comes back in ishizaki s face   cooperation  don t make me laugh  people betray each other with ease  people lie  relationships built on trust just aren t viable  you can only trust yourself   i absolutely loathe hard work  patience  saving  you must be joking   ah  she ran out of here rather suddenly  she went looking for help from another class in the end  pathetic girl  admits her light punishment was a slap   he gestures it   and offers forgiveness only on his terms   if she grovels on the ground  i ll forgive her  i ve a tolerant heart   another boy defied me as well  so i had him driven out  i heard he didn t die  so he s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive  spent the entire three hundred point budget on day one    yes  as you said  i used all of our points    so there is nothing left to penalize   ha ha ha  what should i do  i wonder  well  i suppose that plain  ordinary people can only engage in plain  ordinary thinking  calls her by her first name against her refusal  and answers her disgust while touching himself under the bathing suit   see you later  suzune   well  i rather like forceful women  i ll make you submit to me eventually  when that time comes  it will be the ultimate pleasure  treats his fetch boy as furniture   the warm bottle is thrown back at him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: the beach at zero<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.109–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Holds court on the Class C beach in swimwear — tanned, laid back in his chair, flashing white teeth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ishizaki-daichi\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Just as you see. We&#x27;re enjoying our summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm. Well, I didn&#x27;t make a precise calculation,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Class D, the lowest of all, has to put up with starvation, heat, and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points. It makes me laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pours his remaining water on the sand “almost in provocation” while Ishizaki fetches another bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said to bring me cold water. This water&#x27;s warm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Ryuuen&#x27;s pupils were just like those of a snake.” — the returned bottle comes back in Ishizaki&#x27;s face.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cooperation? Don&#x27;t make me laugh. People betray each other with ease. People lie. Relationships built on trust just aren&#x27;t viable. You can only trust yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I absolutely loathe hard work. Patience? Saving? You must be joking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. She ran out of here rather suddenly. She went looking for help from another class in the end? Pathetic girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Admits her light punishment was a slap — he gestures it — and offers forgiveness only on his terms: “If she grovels on the ground, I&#x27;ll forgive her. I&#x27;ve a tolerant heart.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Another boy defied me as well, so I had him driven out. I heard he didn&#x27;t die, so he&#x27;s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Spent the entire three-hundred-point budget on day one — “Yes, as you said. I used all of our points.” — so there is nothing left to penalize.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha ha. What should I do, I wonder? Well, I suppose that plain, ordinary people can only engage in plain, ordinary thinking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls her by her first name against her refusal, and answers her disgust while touching himself under the bathing suit.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I rather like forceful women. I&#x27;ll make you submit to me eventually. When that time comes, it will be the ultimate pleasure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Treats his fetch-boy as furniture — the warm bottle is thrown back at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.9: collecting the card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 6  6 9  collecting the card answers ibuki s flashlight signal in the wet woods to collect what his operation stole  his spy since the test began   she reports to him over the transceiver and hands the card over   yo  excellent work  ibuki  you did well   naturally  if you hadn t made any mistakes until now  i wouldn t have had to risk coming over here   so  where s the card  checks the engraved name under his flashlight and calls katsuragi out of the shadows to confirm it   you come over here and confirm it  too  that was your condition  remember  relax  it s dark out  and this weather is horrible  there shouldn t be anyone here  it s great to be cautious  but don t waste time  holds her stolen leader card under the flashlight  engraved name up   are you convinced now  untagged  it follows the card and the inspection  so it is recorded as his   don t sit there and think about it forever  the situation is black and white  so make your decision  you re already halfway there  don t do something as stupid as pulling out here  presses the offer with sakayanagi s faction rumor   the student council failure   framed as katsuragi s chance   if this wasn t an honorable deed  then what are you going to do  did you know that sakayanagi s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts  this might be your chance  right   class a maintains its position by forming alliances  if you can form those  even those who have double crossed you will return under your wing  won t they  or you could make me your enemy  i suppose  if you do  i wonder what would happen   that s good  you ve exercised sound judgment   to form an alliance  with class a  takes his handshake on the class a alliance after the pressure   the narration calls it a contract with the devil   i have that covered  of course  he will have no choice but to honor his promise  the answer to ibuki s renege question is untagged  it is his  against her doubt  lays out the contract s terms to ibuki with a creepy smile   the page never quotes them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.9: collecting the card<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.221–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Answers Ibuki’s flashlight signal in the wet woods to collect what his operation stole.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yo. Excellent work, Ibuki. You did well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Naturally? If you hadn’t made any mistakes until now, I wouldn’t have had to risk coming over here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, where’s the card?”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> His spy since the test began — she reports to him over the transceiver and hands the card over.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Checks the engraved name under his flashlight and calls Katsuragi out of the shadows to confirm it.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You come over here and confirm it, too. That was your condition, remember? Relax, it’s dark out, and this weather is horrible. There shouldn’t be anyone here. It’s great to be cautious, but don’t waste time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Holds her stolen leader card under the flashlight, engraved name up.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you convinced now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Untagged; it follows the card and the inspection, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t sit there and think about it forever. The situation is black-and-white, so make your decision. You’re already halfway there. Don’t do something as stupid as pulling out here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Presses the offer with Sakayanagi’s faction rumor — the student-council failure — framed as Katsuragi’s chance.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If this wasn’t an honorable deed, then what are you going to do? Did you know that Sakayanagi’s faction has dominated ever since rumors spread that you failed to get on the student council despite your best efforts? This might be your chance, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class A maintains its position by forming alliances. If you can form those, even those who have double-crossed you will return under your wing, won’t they? Or you could make me your enemy, I suppose? If you do, I wonder what would happen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s good. You’ve exercised sound judgment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To form an alliance. With Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Takes his handshake on the Class A alliance after the pressure — the narration calls it a contract with the devil.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have that covered, of course. He will have no choice but to honor his promise.”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The answer to Ibuki’s renege question is untagged; it is his, against her doubt.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lays out the contract’s terms to Ibuki with a creepy smile — the page never quotes them.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the beach at zero<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p241-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the lone Class C<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p241-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  the lone class c the only class c student left on the beach comes over to provoke the class d trio  hears the results in his face  and later turns up in the lounge retelling as the variable with the most information   oh  hey there  sycophants  what happened to suzune   i know you ve been chasing suzune s ass  we were together before  you know  drains his cup  then crushes it and throws it at ayanokoji s feet   throw that away for me   what a stupid thing to say  huh  pick up your own trash  jerk   but picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage   calm down  sudou kun  here  i ll throw it away   who are you  more importantly  where s suzune  i ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom   the next time you say something stupid  i ll kill you  sudou growled   what are you doing  and  huh  what s with you  getting all excited by yourself  huh  run untagged around sudou s tagged threat and are left out as chapter attribution gaps   horikita san retired yesterday  she s not here   retired  suzune  she doesn t seem like that kind of girl   i thought you retired  ryuuen kun  and the interrupted reply  that s  are left out as chapter attribution gaps  the broken three quarter mark is kept as printed   that s what we should be saying to you class c people  you used up all of your points  right  don t make us laugh   ha  i m jealous of the nerve of you small fry  how you can be satisfied with that amount of points   that s right  i wrote it on the paper  didn t i  the name of class d s leader   also  those guys in a and b wrote the same thing  too  do you know what this means  the page s own reading of the reveal  if the name holds  class d is hit with penalties and loses 100 points   it doesn t really matter whatever you say  class c is still going to stay at zero points  runs untagged between ryuuen s taunts and is left out as a chapter attribution gap   zero  can only watch in silence as the class d trio heads for the boat with sudou s gesture in the air  read as the variable with more information than himself   the identities of all the leaders in hand  classes a and c were connected behind the scenes  class c sacrificed its own points and bought whatever class a needed  and by taking all of c s tools class a spent the week without using any points   ibuki s evidence went to someone in class a  ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact  ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation   no one else controlled it  and his mistake was trusting no one  the test in one line  class a failed on its internal rift  class b ran defense only and paid for believing kaneda  class c sent spies and negotiated with a  and class d avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader  named the number one enemy   spies for the leaders  identities plus whatever the class a negotiations bought","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the lone Class C<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.241–257<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The only Class C student left on the beach comes over to provoke the Class D trio, hears the results in his face, and later turns up in the lounge retelling as the variable with the most information.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, hey there, sycophants. What happened to Suzune?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I know you’ve been chasing Suzune’s ass. We were together before, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Throw that away for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>23 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Drains his cup, then crushes it and throws it at Ayanokōji’s feet.<span class=\"pg\">p.241–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a stupid thing to say. Huh? Pick up your own trash, jerk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, Sudou-kun. Here, I’ll throw it away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you? More importantly, where’s Suzune? I’ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next time you say something stupid, I’ll kill you,” Sudou growled.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “What are you doing?” and “Huh? What’s with you? Getting all excited by yourself, huh?” run untagged around Sudou’s tagged threat and are left out as chapter attribution gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san retired yesterday. She’s not here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Retired? Suzune? She doesn’t seem like that kind of girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I thought you retired, Ryuuen-kun.” and the interrupted reply “That’s¾” are left out as chapter attribution gaps; the broken three-quarter mark is kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what we should be saying to you Class C people. You used up all of your points, right? Don’t make us laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha. I’m jealous of the nerve of you small fry. How you can be satisfied with that amount of points…”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. I wrote it on the paper, didn’t I? The name of Class D’s leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, those guys in A and B wrote the same thing, too. Do you know what this means?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The page’s own reading of the reveal: if the name holds, Class D is hit with penalties and loses 100 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “It doesn’t really matter whatever you say; Class C is still going to stay at zero points.” runs untagged between Ryuuen’s taunts and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Zero?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Can only watch in silence as the Class D trio heads for the boat with Sudou’s gesture in the air.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Read as the variable with more information than himself — the identities of all the leaders in hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Classes A and C were connected behind the scenes: Class C sacrificed its own points and bought whatever Class A needed, and by taking all of C’s tools Class A spent the week without using any points — Ibuki’s evidence went to someone in Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact; Ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation — no one else controlled it, and his mistake was trusting no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The test in one line: Class A failed on its internal rift, Class B ran defense-only and paid for believing Kaneda, Class C sent spies and negotiated with A, and Class D avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Named the number one enemy — spies for the leaders’ identities plus whatever the Class A negotiations bought.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p221-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.9: collecting the card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  2 5  the walk through provocation arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys  sizes up the pond  and picks a fight with katsuragi   well  well  so many fish in this pond  i ve come to take a look for myself   unfortunately  it looks like i m with you   to katsuragi s question whether he belongs to the meeting   how about you put on a little show for me  what do you think of beauty and the beast   looking at both horikita and katsuragi  then letting out a demented little chuckle   academic ability  how droll  that kind of thing is meaningless   hmm  awful attitude  what in the world are you talking about  i can t possibly imagine  can you perhaps tell me how i am  in fact  awful  gestured to his crew as if to ask whether katsuragi s argument was believable   their response mechanical  his three followers wear terrified looks and move docile    more like a king and his servants  the academic society argument ends in a cold stalemate  she flips her hair and turns her back on him to go inside","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.57–60<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives uninvited at the gathering with three terrified lackeys, sizes up the pond, and picks a fight with Katsuragi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, well. So many fish in this pond. I’ve come to take a look for myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Unfortunately, it looks like I’m with you.” (to Katsuragi’s question whether he belongs to the meeting)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How about you put on a little show for me? What do you think of Beauty and the Beast?” (looking at both Horikita and Katsuragi, then letting out a demented little chuckle)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Academic ability? How droll. That kind of thing is meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm? Awful attitude? What in the world are you talking about? I can’t possibly imagine. Can you perhaps tell me how I am, in fact, awful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gestured to his crew as if to ask whether Katsuragi’s argument was believable; “their response mechanical.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His three followers wear terrified looks and move docile — “more like a king and his servants.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The academic-society argument ends in a cold stalemate.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She flips her hair and turns her back on him to go inside.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the Dragon roster and the wariness answer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  the dragon roster and the wariness answer the dragon roster prints his name as the class c seat of horikita s group  listed as ryuuen kakeru in class c with oda takumi  suzuki hidetoshi  and sonoda masashi  the class d line of the same group is kushida  hirata  and horikita  the group read  horikita s inclusion isn t necessarily advantageous   she and ryuuen are especially incompatible  like fire and water  asked who he s most wary of  ayanokoji answers ryuuen  by a mile   after naming katsuragi the most excellent","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the Dragon roster and the wariness answer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64–65, p.67<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Dragon roster prints his name as the Class C seat of Horikita’s group.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Listed as Ryuuen Kakeru in Class C with Oda Takumi, Suzuki Hidetoshi, and Sonoda Masashi; the Class D line of the same group is Kushida, Hirata, and Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The group read: Horikita’s inclusion isn’t necessarily advantageous — she and Ryuuen are especially incompatible, like fire and water.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Asked who he’s most wary of, Ayanokōji answers Ryuuen, by a mile — after naming Katsuragi the most excellent.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p57-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the walk-through provocation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  3 0  the cafe provocation walks into blue ocean with ibuki mid horikita briefing  straddles a vacant seat  and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey   nice weather  eh suzune  you having breakfast with this clingy beta male   you should have received the message already  what were the results  were you chosen as the vip   i suppose you wouldn t give anything away  but that doesn t matter  according to my information  there s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should ve led to victory  said ryuuen   yesterday  it seemed katsuragi was rather cautious of you  he said   heh  well  i won t deny that  i came here to measure your abilities for myself  he answered   katsuragi and i think differently  when i m dealing with someone  i like to keep an eye on them   i m remembering the test on the island  the result  the process that led to it  there are only certain types of people who would ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that  a girl like you is far too serious minded to have come up with it  reasoned ryuuen   katsuragi probably didn t know   his read on who grasped the points flow   at the end of the test  i wrote down your name as leader  but that was wrong  there s just one reason why that was wrong  your class leader changed right before the test ended  the only explanation  mused ryuuen   ah  however  katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing  but was that really the case  in my opinion  you becoming the leader and then retiring were both unexpected  besides  i had my own strategy in place  i had ibuki infiltrate your class to find out the leader s identity  you did nothing to counter that strategy at first  said ryuuen   the key question is who replaced you as leader  personally  i think the second leader was pulling your strings from behind the scenes during the entire test  speaks to horikita but watches ayanokoji the whole time    if i appeared shaken for even an instant  he d pounce   well  i suppose that s expected of a clingy tagalong   that guy with you is considerably smart  despite that  he hasn t achieved anything significant  or gotten high grades  he has some excellent qualities  though i have my doubts  said ryuuen   i see your point  i never imagined you d trip me up  i ll admit it  the results of the test shocked me  answered ryuuen   well  that s too bad  i love surprise attacks  foul play  and subterfuge  that level of strategy was totally unexpected  but your victory high will soon come to an end  whether it s you  suzune  or someone pulling the strings behind the scenes  you re stupid  you ve already made your best move  class d is one or two steps behind the other classes in points  the challenge will only heat up from here  you already played your trump card during the survival test  when the game was just getting started  you couldn t see what was in front of or behind you  i don t think you ll find this round as easy as last time  tell that to whoever helped you ace the test  warned ryuuen   what can i say  i m quite merciful  snaps a photo of horikita without asking  studies the sour expression  and pockets the phone satisfied   someone in class d other than you is quite clever  there s no mistake about that  he said   a conversation reveals many subtle things  i m glad i could talk with you  suzune  it s a game to me  i ll discover who among you is making moves behind the scenes  everyone  including your clingy friend here  is a target  said ryuuen   i already know their abilities  to some extent  neither katsuragi nor ichinose is my enemy  if i wanted to crush them  i could do it any time   i m saving her for the final course  it d be a waste to eat her now  let s go  ibuki  ryuuen stood and left with his lackey   on sakayanagi  the whole visit is reconnaissance  measure horikita  float the hidden second leader theory  and leave without confirming anything   narration says he only wanted to chat and pass the time amusing himself  the target of the visit  he needles her  photographs her  and walks off still doubting her  brings her as the visible lackey and cuts her off when she would snap back  sizes him up as smart but inert and keeps him in the target set without ever addressing him directly  the rival whose caution and island read he quotes back at horikita  saved  for the final course    he will not spend her now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.68–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into Blue Ocean with Ibuki mid-Horikita-briefing, straddles a vacant seat, and spends the coffee working the island result until he leaves with his lackey.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nice weather, eh Suzune? You having breakfast with this clingy beta male?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You should have received the message already. What were the results? Were you chosen as the VIP?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I suppose you wouldn’t give anything away, but that doesn’t matter. According to my information, there’s no way that your farcical bumbling on the island should’ve led to victory,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yesterday, it seemed Katsuragi was rather cautious of you,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. Well, I won’t deny that. I came here to measure your abilities for myself,” he answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi and I think differently. When I’m dealing with someone, I like to keep an eye on them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m remembering the test on the island. The result. The process that led to it. There are only certain types of people who would’ve been able to conceptualize and execute a plan like that. A girl like you is far too serious-minded to have come up with it,” reasoned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi probably didn’t know.” (his read on who grasped the points flow)<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At the end of the test, I wrote down your name as leader, but that was wrong. There’s just one reason why that was wrong: Your class leader changed right before the test ended. The only explanation,” mused Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. However, Katsuragi thinks you planned the whole thing. But was that really the case? In my opinion, you becoming the leader and then retiring were both unexpected. Besides, I had my own strategy in place. I had Ibuki infiltrate your class to find out the leader’s identity. You did nothing to counter that strategy at first,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The key question is who replaced you as leader. Personally, I think the second leader was pulling your strings from behind the scenes during the entire test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Speaks to Horikita but watches Ayanokōji the whole time — “If I appeared shaken for even an instant, he’d pounce.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose that’s expected of a clingy tagalong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That guy with you is considerably smart. Despite that, he hasn’t achieved anything significant, or gotten high grades. He has some excellent qualities, though I have my doubts,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see your point. I never imagined you’d trip me up. I’ll admit it. The results of the test shocked me,” answered Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s too bad. I love surprise attacks, foul play, and subterfuge. That level of strategy was totally unexpected, but your victory high will soon come to an end. Whether it’s you, Suzune, or someone pulling the strings behind the scenes, you’re stupid. You’ve already made your best move. Class D is one or two steps behind the other classes in points. The challenge will only heat up from here. You already played your trump card during the survival test, when the game was just getting started. You couldn’t see what was in front of or behind you. I don’t think you’ll find this round as easy as last time. Tell that to whoever helped you ace the test,” warned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What can I say? I’m quite merciful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Snaps a photo of Horikita without asking, studies the sour expression, and pockets the phone satisfied.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Someone in Class D other than you is quite clever. There’s no mistake about that,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A conversation reveals many subtle things. I’m glad I could talk with you, Suzune. It’s a game to me. I’ll discover who among you is making moves behind the scenes. Everyone, including your clingy friend here, is a target,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already know their abilities, to some extent. Neither Katsuragi nor Ichinose is my enemy. If I wanted to crush them, I could do it any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m saving her for the final course. It’d be a waste to eat her now. Let’s go, Ibuki.” Ryuuen stood and left with his lackey. (on Sakayanagi)<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The whole visit is reconnaissance: measure Horikita, float the hidden-second-leader theory, and leave without confirming anything — narration says he only wanted to chat and pass the time amusing himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The target of the visit; he needles her, photographs her, and walks off still doubting her.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Brings her as the visible lackey and cuts her off when she would snap back.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Sizes him up as smart-but-inert and keeps him in the target set without ever addressing him directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.68, 73–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The rival whose caution and island read he quotes back at Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.70, 72, 75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Saved “for the final course” — he will not spend her now.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the Dragon roster and the wariness answer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p76-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the strategy in motion and the talent bar<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p76-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  the strategy in motion and the talent bar named as the man already moving his new strategy after the cafe interrupt  ibuki s walk with ryuuen reads as his new strategy already being implemented   his showing up here is called dangerous  in the talent comparison  not even katsuragi or ryuuen could match ichinose s de facto leadership","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the strategy in motion and the talent bar<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.76, p.84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the man already moving his new strategy after the café interrupt.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ibuki’s walk with Ryuuen reads as his new strategy already being implemented — his showing up here is called dangerous.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In the talent comparison, not even Katsuragi or Ryuuen could match Ichinose’s de facto leadership.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.0: the café provocation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"hoshinomiya-chie katsuragi-kouhei ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  named twice  absent both times two second half mentions   the kouenji shock list and the teachers  dragon roster talk   katsuragi  ryuuen  and ichinose would all be surprised by this    grouped with them as a leader who had not imagined an early traitor  hoshinomiya s class c complaint   if we evaluated the class   c students properly  another student should ve been placed into dragon  but they threw ryuuen in there  the teacher who thinks the dragon pick was a class c evaluation failure  the other surprised leader on the same line  the third name on the surprise list","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.115, p.123<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two second-half mentions — the Kouenji shock list and the teachers’ Dragon roster talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “Katsuragi, Ryuuen, and Ichinose would all be surprised by this” — grouped with them as a leader who had not imagined an early traitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Hoshinomiya’s Class C complaint: “If we evaluated the Class … C students properly, another student should’ve been placed into Dragon. But they threw Ryuuen in there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122-123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The teacher who thinks the Dragon pick was a Class C evaluation failure.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The other surprised leader on the same line.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The third name on the surprise list.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p76-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the strategy in motion and the talent bar<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  4 0  the shade meeting and the planted phone he drops into horikita and ayanokoji s shade conversation  claims class c can win by rule logic  and leaves a silent recording phone under his own chair   hey  you two  having yourselves a nice date in the shade  let me in on the fun   that s for me to decide  well then  have you decided how to find the vip  he asked   i ve already started to discover the vip s identity  would you believe me if i told you that   well  you re right that i m not a professional friend collector  but making friends has nothing to do with whether or not i can gather information   unfortunately for you  i ve already gotten a handle on the fundamentals of this test  depending on how things go  class c will win by an overwhelming majority   it s an extremely simple matter  all you need to do is find out what   class the vip is from  then  your next move is to analyze the group  said ryuuen   you just have to make sure it s a situation where someone can t lie  he said   i take everyone s cell phones  so if someone lies to me  all i have to do is check everyone s email  one by one  said ryuuen   it s not really a problem at all  actually  i m here because it s not a problem  do you get what i mean  brute force phone seizure as a class c method   no complaints means consent  narration reads it as operating within the rules and as three vips already identified   looks like you finally understand   maybe i m just playing around   now  then  suppose i m about to reach checkmate  he said   i don t think about it at all  i don t really care about small fry  see you again  suzune  dismisses the monkey group early end as small fry  leaves  a silent phone set to record audio stays under his chair with the chat line  sorry for yesterday  parting  see you again  suzune    first name basis  reported","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.128–131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He drops into Horikita and Ayanokōji’s shade conversation, claims Class C can win by rule-logic, and leaves a silent recording phone under his own chair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, you two. Having yourselves a nice date in the shade? Let me in on the fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s for me to decide. Well then, have you decided how to find the VIP?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve already started to discover the VIP’s identity. Would you believe me if I told you that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, you’re right that I’m not a professional friend-collector, but making friends has nothing to do with whether or not I can gather information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately for you, I’ve already gotten a handle on the fundamentals of this test. Depending on how things go, Class C will win by an overwhelming majority.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s an extremely simple matter. All you need to do is find out what … class the VIP is from. Then, your next move is to analyze the group,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You just have to make sure it’s a situation where someone can’t lie,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I take everyone’s cell phones. So if someone lies to me, all I have to do is check everyone’s email, one by one,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not really a problem at all, actually. I’m here because it’s not a problem. Do you get what I mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Brute-force phone seizure as a Class C method — no complaints means consent; narration reads it as operating within the rules and as three VIPs already identified.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like you finally understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe I’m just playing around?”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now, then. Suppose I’m about to reach checkmate?” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think about it at all. I don’t really care about small fry. See you again, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Dismisses the Monkey-group early end as small fry.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Leaves; a silent phone set to record audio stays under his chair with the chat line “Sorry for yesterday!”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Parting “See you again, Suzune” — first-name basis, reported.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named twice, absent both times<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the three-way deadlock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p132-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  the three way deadlock named in the teachers conversation echo that pins the group s academic shape   then stays in the dragon room as ichinose and ayanokoji wait outside  the overheard teacher talk and what ryuuen had said leave no doubt about the pure academic ranking of the room  the narration contrasts the respectful class b table with the type of relationship katsuragi and ryuuen have with their subjects  ichinose can t imagine ryuuen and katsuragi holding a discussion   maybe class b is showing off their power  all of the class c students leave the room except ryuuen  kushida reports they re still discussing things with ryuuen kun  inside  horikita  kanzaki  and ryuuen sit slightly apart   a three way deadlock  ryuuen needles ayanokouji on sniffing around chicks   first suzune  now ichinose   and presses ichinose on landing in the losers  group  he floats the proposal to crush class a  claims to already know all the class c vip identities  and the narration calls it a very ryuuen like plan  even if suzune wanted to agree  there s a reason she can t   he s willing to leave classes a and d stripped bare  the ichinose ryuuen team up reads as extremely dangerous  he mocks ayanokouji as tagalong and gets his honest opinion back  after ichinose refuses on class b s sake  he answers that it s unfortunate without looking disappointed   as if he d guessed her answer  ichinose judges ryuuen kun s plan will fail and names katsuragi s iron fortress the real problem instead  the comparison  anyone else could have gotten her class on board without scare tactics like ryuuen  the three way contrast ends with ryuuen  who wanted to turn everyone into his enemy while taking complete control","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the three-way deadlock<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.132, p.139–150, p.153, p.159<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the teachers’-conversation echo that pins the group’s academic shape — then stays in the Dragon room as Ichinose and Ayanokōji wait outside.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The overheard teacher talk and what Ryuuen had said leave no doubt about the pure-academic ranking of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration contrasts the respectful Class B table with the type of relationship Katsuragi and Ryuuen have with their subjects.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose can’t imagine Ryuuen and Katsuragi holding a discussion — maybe Class B is showing off their power.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> All of the Class C students leave the room except Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida reports they’re still discussing things with Ryuuen-kun; inside, Horikita, Kanzaki, and Ryuuen sit slightly apart — a three-way deadlock.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen needles Ayanokouji on sniffing around chicks — first Suzune, now Ichinose — and presses Ichinose on landing in the losers’ group.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He floats the proposal to crush Class A, claims to already know all the Class C VIP identities, and the narration calls it a very Ryuuen-like plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Even if Suzune wanted to agree, there’s a reason she can’t — he’s willing to leave Classes A and D stripped bare.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The Ichinose–Ryuuen team-up reads as extremely dangerous; he mocks Ayanokouji as tagalong and gets his honest opinion back.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After Ichinose refuses on Class B’s sake, he answers that it’s unfortunate without looking disappointed — as if he’d guessed her answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose judges Ryuuen-kun’s plan will fail and names Katsuragi’s iron fortress the real problem instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The comparison: anyone else could have gotten her class on board without scare tactics like Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The three-way contrast ends with Ryuuen, who wanted to turn everyone into his enemy while taking complete control.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the shade meeting and the planted phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p184-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the unsure answer and the Class C threat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p184-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  the unsure answer and the class c threat named in the closing doubts about who really understood the school s rules  ryuuen claimed he understood the rules  but the test hadn t ended for anyone other than the cow group   proof he didn t have a sure answer either  his class c is the external threat in ayanokoji s warning  if manabe s group carried on with karuizawa  they would cause trouble for ryuuen and land in jeopardy themselves","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the unsure answer and the Class C threat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.184, p.202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the closing doubts about who really understood the school’s rules.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen claimed he understood the rules, but the test hadn’t ended for anyone other than the Cow group — proof he didn’t have a sure answer either.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His Class C is the external threat in Ayanokōji’s warning: if Manabe’s group carried on with Karuizawa, they would cause trouble for Ryuuen and land in jeopardy themselves.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the three-way deadlock<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 5  5 0  the frontal assault still running named in the final day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate   united frontal assault against katsuragi s fortress  the two strategies ichinose has not answered  the chapter opens between them  still the fear she won t detail under listener risk at the 5 1 meet  no scene presence in this half  the row records the opening status line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the final-day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate — united frontal assault against Katsuragi’s fortress.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The two strategies Ichinose has not answered; the chapter opens between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Still the fear she won’t detail under listener risk at the 5.1 meet.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence in this half; the row records the opening status line.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p184-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the unsure answer and the Class C threat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth guest<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 5  5 3  the sixth guest invited as the deliberate sixth seat  slams a chair beside horikita  names kushida as dragon vip from her body language  shows the class a vip list  claims the four email timing  and declares horikita his next target  the whole set piece is aimed at her   teasing  the reveal   you re my next target  tear you to shreds  both in mind and body   i thought i d enjoy finding out the results with you all  thanks so much for gathering in such an easy to find place  he said mockingly   anyway  suzune  you ve got a rather large group with you  have you grown more sociable  muttered ryuuen  looking out at the other four people gathered around the table and ignoring sudou completely  ignored on arrival  sudou s chide about the last results is brushed into the kushida play   i didn t think you actually had any friends  ryuuen teased   the results will be announced any minute now  are you expecting any results  he asked   heh  i wouldn t be here if i wasn t  looks like the same crowd as the last time  replied ryuuen   stop it  suzune  you know if you get carried away now  you ll just be embarrassed later  i already know our group s vip  said ryuuen   there s no need to wait for the announcement  want me to tell you who the dragon group vip is  he asked   if you could only understand the depth of my mercy  you d be moved  so moved that you ll get wet between your thighs  ryuuen laughed  as though such vulgar language was funny   kushida kikyou  the name dropped cold   known since the second day of the test   i m sorry  but i ve known kushida was the vip since the second day of the test  ryuuen said   i just felt so sorry for you  you were oh so incredibly confident in your victory that you looked down on others  you were desperate to get your stories straight  assuming no one would get the answer right  that s why i went along with it until the end  hirata s  how did you figure it out  carries curiosity and fear  the answer names horikita  not him   unfortunately  the answer to that  well  it involves you  suzune  answered ryuuen   i figured it out because of your body  the movements of your eyes and mouth  your breathing  your behavior  your tone  everything about you told me that you were lying  continued ryuuen in an eerie voice  body language read of horikita s lie   the method that beat the vip secret   jokes  if it s a joke  then how do i know the truth   i understand how you feel  you don t want to admit that you re the most incompetent person in the group  but don t beat yourself up  suzune  you merely chose the wrong opponent  besides  this exam was supposed to be pure chaos  at any rate  class a is in for an especially rude awakening  relax   you ll understand soon enough  the four simultaneous betrayal emails   rat  horse  monkey  rooster answered correctly  he played a major part  class a vip list on his screen for rat  rooster and pig   isn t this great  suzune  thanks to your blunder  the dragon group managed to clear this test with outcome  1  because of that  all the classes should receive a boost in points  ryuuen crowed  he clapped his hands and wore a satisfied grin   if you beg for it  i ll tell you the answer  how about it  he asked   ooh  that look you have  it s pretty sexy   i made some adjustments and arrived at the root of the test  then  i just focused on the class a students  he said  cleared without targeting classes b or d at all   the class a vip harvest on one screen   i m sorry to tell you  suzune  but you re my next target  i m going after you with everything i ve got  i won t stop until i tear you to shreds  both in mind and body   i m looking forward to the second semester  said ryuuen  walks away with his payback for the island   the threat ayanokoji turns into quiet excitement  the defensive vote he bent to 1    named in ayanokoji s explanation of dragon outcome  1","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.3: the sixth guest<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.237–243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Invited as the deliberate sixth seat, slams a chair beside Horikita, names Kushida as Dragon VIP from her body language, shows the Class A VIP list, claims the four-email timing, and declares Horikita his next target.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I thought I’d enjoy finding out the results with you all. Thanks so much for gathering in such an easy-to-find place,” he said mockingly.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Anyway, Suzune, you’ve got a rather large group with you. Have you grown more sociable?” muttered Ryuuen, looking out at the other four people gathered around the table and ignoring Sudou completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I didn’t think you actually had any friends,” Ryuuen teased.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The whole set piece is aimed at her — teasing, the reveal, “you’re my next target… tear you to shreds, both in mind and body.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Ignored on arrival; Sudou’s chide about the last results is brushed into the Kushida play.<span class=\"pg\">p.238-239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The results will be announced any minute now. Are you expecting any results?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. I wouldn’t be here if I wasn’t. Looks like the same crowd as the last time,” replied Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop it, Suzune. You know if you get carried away now, you’ll just be embarrassed later. I already know our group’s VIP,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no need to wait for the announcement. Want me to tell you who the Dragon group VIP is?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you could only understand the depth of my mercy, you’d be moved. So moved that you’ll get wet between your thighs.” Ryuuen laughed, as though such vulgar language was funny.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida Kikyou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The name dropped cold — known since the second day of the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I’ve known Kushida was the VIP since the second day of the test,” Ryuuen said.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I just felt so sorry for you. You were oh-so-incredibly confident in your victory that you looked down on others. You were desperate to get your stories straight, assuming no one would get the answer right. That’s why I went along with it until the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata’s “How did you figure it out?” carries curiosity and fear; the answer names Horikita, not him.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, the answer to that… Well, it involves you, Suzune,” answered Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I figured it out because of your body. The movements of your eyes and mouth. Your breathing. Your behavior. Your tone. Everything about you told me that you were lying,” continued Ryuuen in an eerie voice.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Body-language read of Horikita’s lie — the method that beat the VIP secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Jokes? If it’s a joke, then how do I know the truth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand how you feel. You don’t want to admit that you’re the most incompetent person in the group. But don’t beat yourself up, Suzune. You merely chose the wrong opponent. Besides, this exam was supposed to be pure chaos. At any rate, Class A is in for an especially rude awakening. Relax.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ll understand soon enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The four simultaneous betrayal emails — Rat, Horse, Monkey, Rooster answered correctly; he played a major part; Class A VIP list on his screen for Rat, Rooster and Pig.<span class=\"pg\">p.240-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t this great, Suzune? Thanks to your blunder, the Dragon group managed to clear this test with Outcome #1. Because of that, all the classes should receive a boost in points,” Ryuuen crowed. He clapped his hands and wore a satisfied grin. “If you beg for it, I’ll tell you the answer. How about it?” he asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ooh, that look you have. It’s pretty sexy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I made some adjustments and arrived at the root of the test. Then, I just focused on the Class A students,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Cleared without targeting Classes B or D at all — the Class A VIP harvest on one screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry to tell you, Suzune, but you’re my next target. I’m going after you with everything I’ve got. I won’t stop until I tear you to shreds, both in mind and body.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m looking forward to the second semester,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Walks away with his payback for the island — the threat Ayanokōji turns into quiet excitement.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The defensive vote he bent to 1% — named in Ayanokōji’s explanation of Dragon Outcome #1.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0: the frontal assault still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p23-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  a passing mention in ibuki s refusal named only as the man ibuki will not look at on a holiday   i hate seeing his face  even when i have to  their ship pairing was atonement for her failure to discover class d s leader    that was because it was my fault that i didn t discover class d s leader  she answered quietly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in Ibuki’s refusal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only as the man Ibuki will not look at on a holiday.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I hate seeing his face, even when I have to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Their ship pairing was atonement for her failure to discover Class D’s leader — “That was because it was my fault that I didn’t discover Class D’s leader,” she answered quietly.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p24-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  a passing mention ryuen is named as the partner option already ruled out in ibuki s hunt","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryūen is named as the partner option already ruled out in Ibuki&#x27;s hunt.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p23-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in Ibuki’s refusal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p31-1\">→ After: Ch.2: a passing mention in the queue talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p31-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  a passing mention in the queue talk named twice in the narration sizing up ibuki s standing with him  she caught his eye early on  after the spy identity broke she was at his side on several occasions   atonement for her failure  but he trusted her  at least to some degree","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: a passing mention in the queue talk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.31<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named twice in the narration sizing up Ibuki’s standing with him.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She caught his eye early on; after the spy identity broke she was at his side on several occasions — atonement for her failure, but he trusted her, at least to some degree.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p86-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  a passing mention horikita raises his class c again  the group suffered at ryuuen kun s hands  his win is what still makes her uneasy at the start of the second semester","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.86<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita raises his Class C again: the group suffered at Ryuuen-kun&#x27;s hands.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> His win is what still makes her uneasy at the start of the second semester.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p31-1\">← Before: Ch.2: a passing mention in the queue talk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.4: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p121-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  a passing mention ayanokoji guesses the water thief was ryuen or katsuragi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.121<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji guesses the water thief was Ryūen or Katsuragi.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.3: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p122-1\">→ After: Ch.4: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p122-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  a passing mention ak privately guesses ryuuen or katsuragi forced the dragon group s ship exam outcome  he can t tell which of the two it was  the guess stays in his head","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p122-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.122<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK privately guesses Ryuuen or Katsuragi forced the Dragon group&#x27;s ship-exam outcome.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He can&#x27;t tell which of the two it was; the guess stays in his head.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v4_5-p121-1\">← Before: Ch.4: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2 9  passing mentions named across strategy  festival and trap margins outside his own scene cards  hirata   i think ryuuen kun figured it all out in the middle of the test  ryuuen kun rules class c alone   perhaps that isn t actually true  a traitor defied him  coin flip thought  ryuuen and ayanokouji as tails  class b refused to cooperate with ryuuen  horikita   i assume ryuuen kun was involved somehow  in the vip leak  third group on the starting line boasts students with a strong presence like ryuuen or katsuragi  sakayanagi s behavior is unsettling in a different way than ryuuen s  ryuuen turned his back after the tug of war  he put a damper on the win  male students gather around ryuuen as if he were a king holding court  sudou is unsettled by his tactics   ryuuen probably ordered that  scumbag    sudou on the horikita targeting  class c s general ryuuen laughs fearlessly as d a horsemen rush him  yamada protects ryuuen in the center  hirata grabs ryuuen s headband and it slips  only ryuuen kakeru would prioritize humiliating horikita  he has the full participation table  strategies reveal ryuuen kakeru  foul play only after careful rehearsal  all ryuuen s provocation   stepping on sudou to targeting horikita   sees sudou storm toward class c   something interesting  huh  i ll be looking forward to it  ryuuen says of hirata s promise  traitor leaked the table to ryuuen kun  ryuuen provoked sudou on purpose  counterattack math  ryuuen took out sudou  so the class must rebuild around hirata   looks like ryuuen kun s making his move  as expected  said hirata  horikita was about to say it was part of ryuuen kun s strategy when ayanokouji spoke  whether it was ryuuen kun s strategy or an accident  she could not lie to the teacher  ryuuen kun and kinoshita san both leave after the nurse s office confrontation  ryuuen got hold of the participation table  he wants her to kneel for a million points  no use telling her brother about ryuuen kun  the humiliation stays with her  ayanokouji  if she had hit ryuuen kun  she might have been disqualified  ryuuen kun had defeated her  the brother had abandoned her  cruise ship vip  she asked ryuuen for a favor in exchange for telling everyone she was the vip  ryuuen kun was getting all her points using blackmail after the substitute burden  the behind the scenes tactic was particularly effective against someone like ryuuen  she prepared to respond to ryuuen kun  he had her dancing in the palm of his hand","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2–9: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13–14, 33, 69, 88, 106, 110, 119, 121, 124, 127–128, 130–132, 136–138, 141, 146–147, 156–158, 163, 165, 174, 176, 190, 194<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named across strategy, festival and trap margins outside his own scene cards.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>29 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata: “I think Ryuuen-kun figured it all out in the middle of the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen-kun rules Class C alone — perhaps that isn’t actually true; a traitor defied him.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Coin-flip thought: Ryuuen and Ayanokouji as tails; Class B refused to cooperate with Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita: “I assume Ryuuen-kun was involved somehow” in the VIP leak.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Third group on the starting line boasts students with a strong presence like Ryuuen or Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakayanagi’s behavior is unsettling in a different way than Ryuuen’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen turned his back after the tug-of-war; he put a damper on the win.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Male students gather around Ryuuen as if he were a king holding court; Sudou is unsettled by his tactics.<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Ryuuen probably ordered that. Scumbag!” — Sudou on the Horikita-targeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Class C’s general Ryuuen laughs fearlessly as D/A horsemen rush him.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yamada protects Ryuuen in the center; Hirata grabs Ryuuen’s headband and it slips.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Only Ryuuen Kakeru would prioritize humiliating Horikita; he has the full participation table.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Strategies reveal Ryuuen Kakeru: foul play only after careful rehearsal.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> All Ryuuen’s provocation — stepping on Sudou to targeting Horikita — sees Sudou storm toward Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Something interesting, huh? I’ll be looking forward to it,” Ryuuen says of Hirata’s promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Traitor leaked the table to Ryuuen-kun; Ryuuen provoked Sudou on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Counterattack math: Ryuuen took out Sudou, so the class must rebuild around Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Looks like Ryuuen-kun’s making his move, as expected,” said Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita was about to say it was part of Ryuuen-kun’s strategy when Ayanokouji spoke.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Whether it was Ryuuen-kun’s strategy or an accident, she could not lie to the teacher.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen-kun and Kinoshita-san both leave after the nurse’s office confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen got hold of the participation table; he wants her to kneel for a million points.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No use telling her brother about Ryuuen-kun; the humiliation stays with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokouji: if she had hit Ryuuen-kun, she might have been disqualified.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen-kun had defeated her; the brother had abandoned her.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Cruise-ship VIP: she asked Ryuuen for a favor in exchange for telling everyone she was the VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen-kun was getting all her points using blackmail after the substitute burden.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The behind-the-scenes tactic was particularly effective against someone like Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She prepared to respond to Ryuuen-kun; he had her dancing in the palm of his hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: the walkout<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami manabe-shiho katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  2 2  the walkout when ichinose asks why class c won t discuss strategy  he turns with his hands in his pockets and leads the whole class out of the gym   it s a waste of time   you should be grateful   hmm  i wonder    to ichinose s challenge on winning without cooperating  refuses her cooperation talk to her face  the exit confirms class c s dictatorship  manabe follows him out after the glance back at karuizawa  katsuragi s warning to horikita is keyed to him  he ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant  ayanokoji s read  always looking to win  possibly already holding one or more festival tactics behind the b and c refusal  the walkout confirms his hold on class c inside the volume s first pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the walkout<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.27–28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">When Ichinose asks why Class C won’t discuss strategy, he turns with his hands in his pockets and leads the whole class out of the gym.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s a waste of time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You should be grateful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm, I wonder.” — to Ichinose’s challenge on winning without cooperating.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Refuses her cooperation talk to her face; the exit confirms Class C’s dictatorship.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Manabe follows him out after the glance-back at Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi’s warning to Horikita is keyed to him: he’ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ayanokōji’s read: always looking to win, possibly already holding one or more festival tactics behind the B-and-C refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The walkout confirms his hold on Class C inside the volume’s first pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2–9: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The reconnaissance that isn’t<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 4  4  the reconnaissance that isn t ayanokoji and horikita discuss ryuuen at the edge of the first practice  not one class c student is watching d  she reads the silence as a strategy already in place    reconnaissance isn t necessary for him  the tell is that he isn t hiding it  making the absence of reconnaissance obvious is itself the display  ryuuen s non scouting reads as a message to the other classes  not as disinterest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4: The reconnaissance that isn’t<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji and Horikita discuss Ryuuen at the edge of the first practice: not one Class C student is watching D.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She reads the silence as a strategy already in place — “Reconnaissance isn’t necessary for him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The tell is that he isn’t hiding it: making the absence of reconnaissance obvious is itself the display.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Ryuuen’s non-scouting reads as a message to the other classes, not as disinterest.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the walkout<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 5  5  named in the cruise ship theory ryuuen is the first name in ayanokoji s theory about how the vip identity leaked  horikita s own dead end   i assume ryuuen kun was involved somehow  horikita puts the direct question to kushida   did she tell ryuuen or katsuragi she was the vip  the theory holds that ryuuen was one party  a second  inside class d  was significantly involved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen is the first name in Ayanokōji’s theory about how the VIP identity leaked.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita’s own dead end: “I assume Ryuuen-kun was involved somehow,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Horikita puts the direct question to Kushida — did she tell Ryuuen or Katsuragi she was the VIP?<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The theory holds that Ryuuen was one party; a second, inside Class D, was significantly involved.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4: The reconnaissance that isn’t<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: foul play and the forfeit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 6  6  foul play and the forfeit ryuuen leads class c into the boys  capture the flag against the d a coalition  laughing from the rear like a general  stomps sudou s back as he guards the flag   a low blow the referee culture will call heat of the moment   oh  i didn t notice you  replied ryuuen  he picked up the flag without any hesitation  drops him  takes the flag  and draws a vow of revenge that katsuragi and ayanokoji have to talk down  re forms class c shortest in front into a bow shape after the first tug round loss and threatens them into leverage   if you lose here  i ll kill you  warned ryuuen  lets go of the rope in the third round so the d a side tumbles  calls it a break because they could not win   i decided to take a break  since i thought we couldn t win  said ryuuen   you managed to pick up a meaningless win  is read by katsuragi as wasting their energy and trying to provoke a foul  he turns his back when provocation yields nothing  violence and psychological games are interchangeable tools  even a lost round is a chance to tilt the opponents","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: foul play and the forfeit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.100–110<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen leads Class C into the boys’ capture the flag against the D/A coalition, laughing from the rear like a general.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, I didn’t notice you,” replied Ryuuen. He picked up the flag without any hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you lose here, I’ll kill you,” warned Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I decided to take a break, since I thought we couldn’t win,” said Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stomps Sudou’s back as he guards the flag — a low blow the referee culture will call heat-of-the-moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Drops him, takes the flag, and draws a vow of revenge that Katsuragi and Ayanokōji have to talk down.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Re-forms Class C shortest-in-front into a bow shape after the first tug round loss and threatens them into leverage.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lets go of the rope in the third round so the D/A side tumbles; calls it a break because they could not win.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You managed to pick up a meaningless win.”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Is read by Katsuragi as wasting their energy and trying to provoke a foul; he turns his back when provocation yields nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Violence and psychological games are interchangeable tools; even a lost round is a chance to tilt the opponents.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5: Named in the cruise-ship theory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6: the cavalry crown and the bait<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 6  6  the cavalry crown and the bait ryuuen s class c horsemen ignore class a and take horikita alone in the girls  cavalry   the crush plan made visible  orders the four on one  class c wipes the remaining a d units after her headband falls  sole target  ayanokoji reads it as humiliation for its own sake  not points  rides as class c s general on yamada s power  absorbs sudou s hits  wins the one on one bait  and keeps the sticky headband secret   oh  i remember your name  sudou   oh  i guess this is all meaningless  unless we settle things one onone   if you can only beat me when it s two against one  i suppose that s that   tough words  but with nothing to back them up   if you re so very strong  then face me one on one  studies him  offers the kneel  then wins when hirata s grip fails on the treated cloth   i don t know what you re talking about   if there s anything on my headband  it s probably just hair gel  don t be a sore loser  approaches the tent to ask after sudou while knowing exactly what happened  takes first in the 200 metre dash   hirata  what happened to sudou  he taking a dump   heh  i really don t think lying suits you  is told the leak is known  answers that the class gap fills d with despair and looks forward to hirata s  something interesting   guess luck is on my side   ooh  i d be scared if that weren t such an obvious bluff  psychological harm over raw score  target the leader  bait the hot head  poison the cloth  then smile through the accusation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6: the cavalry crown and the bait<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.120–136<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen’s Class C horsemen ignore Class A and take Horikita alone in the girls’ cavalry — the crush plan made visible.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, I remember your name. Sudou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh? I guess this is all meaningless, unless we settle things one-onone,”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you can only beat me when it’s two against one, I suppose that’s that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Orders the four-on-one; Class C wipes the remaining A/D units after her headband falls.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sole target; Ayanokōji reads it as humiliation for its own sake, not points.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–123, 130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Rides as Class C’s general on Yamada’s power; absorbs Sudou’s hits, wins the one-on-one bait, and keeps the sticky headband secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–129, boys’ cavalry<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tough words, but with nothing to back them up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re so very strong, then face me one-on-one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Studies him, offers the kneel, then wins when Hirata’s grip fails on the treated cloth.<span class=\"pg\">p.125–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If there’s anything on my headband, it’s probably just hair gel. Don’t be a sore loser,”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Approaches the tent to ask after Sudou while knowing exactly what happened; takes first in the 200-metre dash.<span class=\"pg\">p.135, §6.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata, what happened to Sudou? He taking a dump?”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Heh. I really don’t think lying suits you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Is told the leak is known; answers that the class gap fills D with despair and looks forward to Hirata’s “something interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Guess luck is on my side.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ooh. I’d be scared if that weren’t such an obvious bluff.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Psychological harm over raw score: target the leader, bait the hot head, poison the cloth, then smile through the accusation.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: foul play and the forfeit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: arrives at the infirmary<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 1  arrives at the infirmary ryuuen struts into the hallway and then the infirmary to inspect kinoshita s leg   looks like things have gotten really serious   i rushed over after kinoshita asked for me  to think someone did this on purpose   hey  kinoshita  you all right  looks like you ve had a rough time   whoa  this looks bad  i m impressed you ve held up  considering all you re dealing with","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.1: arrives at the infirmary<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.148–149<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen struts into the hallway and then the infirmary to inspect Kinoshita’s leg.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Looks like things have gotten really serious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I rushed over after Kinoshita asked for me. To think someone did this on purpose…”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, Kinoshita. You all right? Looks like you’ve had a rough time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whoa, this looks bad. I’m impressed you’ve held up, considering all you’re dealing with.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6: the cavalry crown and the bait<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: builds the case, demands a million points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 1  builds the case  demands a million points ryuuen turns the collision into intent  then offers to withdraw the complaint for a million points   don t blame yourself  kinoshita  i know you wanted to participate in the three legged race   you really did this on purpose  didn t you   you can never really know someone  can you  convenient  isn t it   it s clear you did this  isn t it   i don t have the time to drag this out   we can strike a quick deal  though   you should compensate kinoshita and class c for any losses   if you hand over a million points  i ll have kinoshita withdraw her complaint   then go ahead and prove that  suzune  lay it all out in black and white for us   we can prove that we aren t lying  let s hurry up and have the student council president render his judgment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.1: builds the case, demands a million points<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.151–153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen turns the collision into intent, then offers to withdraw the complaint for a million points.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t blame yourself, Kinoshita. I know you wanted to participate in the three-legged race,”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You really did this on purpose, didn’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You can never really know someone, can you? Convenient, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s clear you did this, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t have the time to drag this out,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can strike a quick deal, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should compensate Kinoshita and Class C for any losses.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you hand over a million points, I’ll have Kinoshita withdraw her complaint.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then go ahead and prove that, Suzune. Lay it all out in black and white for us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can prove that we aren’t lying. Let’s hurry up and have the student council president render his judgment,”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p148-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: arrives at the infirmary<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.1: the kneeling condition and the deadline<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7  7 1  the kneeling condition and the deadline ryuuen refuses kushida s points  orders the report upward  then adds a kneeling demand after horikita agrees to pay   oh  that s quaint  sorry using your points is a no go   very well  kinoshita  we re going to report this to the teachers  then to the student council   you re admitting to foul play   did you hear that  kinoshita  she doesn t think she s in the wrong  can you forgive her   how about you get down on your knees and beg   teachers should stay out of this  it s a problem between students   kushida  bring suzune to me after the festival  provokes horikita by naming her brother  the student council president  as the judge  deadline after the festival  kneel and pay a million points  or let the school deliberate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.1: the kneeling condition and the deadline<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.154–156<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen refuses Kushida’s points, orders the report upward, then adds a kneeling demand after Horikita agrees to pay.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, that’s quaint. Sorry—using your points is a no-go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Very well. Kinoshita, we’re going to report this to the teachers, then to the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re admitting to foul play?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you hear that, Kinoshita? She doesn’t think she’s in the wrong. Can you forgive her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about you get down on your knees and beg?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Teachers should stay out of this. It’s a problem between students,”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida, bring Suzune to me after the festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Provokes Horikita by naming her brother, the student council president, as the judge.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Deadline after the festival: kneel and pay a million points, or let the school deliberate.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p151-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: builds the case, demands a million points<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1\">→ After: Ch.8 §8: checks on Sudou’s absence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 8  8  checks on sudou s absence ryuuen needles ayanokouji about sudou and horikita both being missing before the scavenger hunt   so  that muscle headed moron won t be participating in the scavenger hunt  huh  i thought he d take part for sure  suzune s not here  either  they couldn t be doing each other backstage  right   what a shitty answer  named by kushida as the man she gambled with on the vip scheme  she calls him a liar who entraps people  horikita tells sudou ryuuen has thoroughly beaten her and holds her points by blackmail","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8 §8: checks on Sudou’s absence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.161<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen needles Ayanokouji about Sudou and Horikita both being missing before the scavenger hunt.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, that muscle-headed moron won’t be participating in the scavenger hunt, huh? I thought he’d take part for sure. Suzune’s not here, either. They couldn’t be doing each other backstage, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What a shitty answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named by Kushida as the man she gambled with on the VIP scheme; she calls him a liar who entraps people.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita tells Sudou Ryuuen has thoroughly beaten her and holds her points by blackmail.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p154-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.1: the kneeling condition and the deadline<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p182-1\">→ After: Ch.9 §9: watches the relay plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p182-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hira-ta ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 9  9  watches the relay plan named in hirata s talk as the rival ryuuen must not beat them again  hirata s line about hating to lose to ryuuen again   recorded under hirata s row","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p182-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 §9: watches the relay plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.182–183<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Hirata’s talk as the rival Ryuuen must not beat them again.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">hira-ta<\/b> Hirata’s line about hating to lose to Ryuuen again — recorded under Hirata’s row.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p161-1\">← Before: Ch.8 §8: checks on Sudou’s absence<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p195-1\">→ After: Ch.9 §9.3: the full confession and the counter-recording<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p195-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kinoshita-minori ayanokouji-kiyotaka ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 9  9 3  the full confession and the counter recording ryuuen receives horikita at the appointment  praises her for not running  then lays out the whole festival plot   until a recording of his own trap plan arrives   so  you didn t run away  suzune  you came   you ve got a good heart  you ve become a finer woman than before   heh heh  what a shrewd woman  well  i guess i decided to work with you because i like this side of your personality   that s really a shame  suzune  he told me   betrayed by such a trustworthy ally   kinoshita running into you earlier was a total accident  she didn t have any ulterior motive or ill intent  that s just the way the world is   i wanted to crush you  that was reason enough  i had no interest in winning the sports festival   before the sports festival  i had kushida get her hands on class d s complete participation table   that s why i had her carefully practice hitting an opponent and making the fall look completely natural   before she got medical treatment  i injured her myself  like this   she agreed when i told her that i d pay her 500 000 points  man  the power of money is a terrifying thing  isn t it  paid 500 000 points to stage the serious injury after the collision   did you come up with that bluff just now   the contents of our current conversation are  at best  complete fiction  i was just humoring your delusions   do you know what this is  the full audio recording  from beginning to end  in fact  i actually took video   abandon your pride and get on your knees  suzune   i see  i see  i see  i see now  heh heh  isn t that interesting  do you know what this means  kikyou  there s a traitor in class c  too   you were used  kikyou  they predicted that you d betray your class and leak the participation table  they read us like a book   well  he s one candidate  but i m not drawing any conclusions yet   i ve failed to get points from suzune or have her kneel  but i m happy with all that i procured  names ayanokouji as one candidate for the recording  will investigate thoroughly  stomps the staged injury confession on tape  then loses the exchange when a counter recording of his trap plan arrives by email   passing mention   p 128  hirata grabs ryuuen s headband and it slips  ryuuen counter grabs","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p195-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 §9.3: the full confession and the counter-recording<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.195–201<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ryuuen receives Horikita at the appointment, praises her for not running, then lays out the whole festival plot — until a recording of his own trap plan arrives.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kinoshita-minori.html\">Kinoshita Minori<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, you didn’t run away, Suzune. You came,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’ve got a good heart. You’ve become a finer woman than before,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Heh heh. What a shrewd woman. Well, I guess I decided to work with you because I like this side of your personality.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s really a shame, Suzune,” he told me. “Betrayed by such a trustworthy ally.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kinoshita running into you earlier was a total accident. She didn’t have any ulterior motive or ill intent. That’s just the way the world is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to crush you. That was reason enough. I had no interest in winning the sports festival,”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Before the sports festival, I had Kushida get her hands on Class D’s complete participation table.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s why I had her carefully practice hitting an opponent and making the fall look completely natural,”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Before she got medical treatment, I injured her myself. Like this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She agreed when I told her that I’d pay her 500,000 points. Man, the power of money is a terrifying thing, isn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kinoshita Minori<\/b> Paid 500,000 points to stage the serious injury after the collision.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you come up with that bluff just now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The contents of our current conversation are, at best, complete fiction. I was just humoring your delusions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you know what this is? The full audio recording, from beginning to end. In fact, I actually took video.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Abandon your pride and get on your knees, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. I see, I see. I see now! Heh heh! Isn’t that interesting? Do you know what this means, Kikyou? There’s a traitor in Class C, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were used, Kikyou. They predicted that you’d betray your class and leak the participation table. They read us like a book.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, he’s one candidate, but I’m not drawing any conclusions yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve failed to get points from Suzune or have her kneel, but I’m happy with all that I procured,”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names Ayanokouji as one candidate for the recording; will investigate thoroughly.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Stomps the staged-injury confession on tape, then loses the exchange when a counter-recording of his trap plan arrives by email. [passing mention] (p.128) Hirata grabs Ryuuen’s headband and it slips; Ryuuen counter-grabs.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v5-p182-1\">← Before: Ch.9 §9: watches the relay plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v6-p22-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"narration spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 2  2 1  named as the shared enemy katsuragi s corridor warning makes him the subject  blackmail  violence  and a past team up   he ll do anything for the sake of winning  even if that means resorting to blackmail or violence  katsuragi regrets having gotten involved with him and says ryuuen is everyone s enemy  ayanokouji recalls the team up rumor  ayanokouji promises to pass katsuragi s warning to horikita  narration  ryuuen is the one pulling manabe s strings from behind the scenes  a confrontation may be nigh  does not appear in person on these pages   named in dialogue and inner recollection only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v6-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: named as the shared enemy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.22–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi’s corridor warning makes him the subject: blackmail, violence, and a past team-up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “He’ll do anything for the sake of winning. Even if that means resorting to blackmail or violence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">Does not appear in person on these pages — named in dialogue and inner recollection only.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi regrets having gotten involved with him and says Ryuuen is everyone’s enemy; Ayanokouji recalls the team-up rumor.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokouji promises to pass Katsuragi’s warning to Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Narration: Ryuuen is the one pulling Manabe’s strings from behind the scenes; a confrontation may be nigh.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v6-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3: watcher, ally, recording target<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v6-p40-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 3  watcher  ally  recording target inner note  ryuuen wants the identity of the person pulling horikita s strings after the relay  already formed an alliance with kushida to entrap horikita  the sports festival recording is put to him  horikita warns he now has ayanokouji on his list   all i did was ensure that ryuuen s plans were crushed    the class c strategy talk was recorded   what did you do to ryuuen kun at the sports festival  narration only  manabe s cruise harassment of karuizawa is the unspoken source of his class c access  does not appear in person on these pages","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v6-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: watcher, ally, recording target<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.40, 48, 50–51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Inner note: Ryuuen wants the identity of the person pulling Horikita’s strings after the relay.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What did you do to Ryuuen-kun at the sports festival?”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Already formed an alliance with Kushida to entrap Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The sports-festival recording is put to him; Horikita warns he now has Ayanokouji on his list.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “All I did was ensure that Ryuuen’s plans were crushed” — the Class C strategy talk was recorded.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Narration only: Manabe’s cruise harassment of Karuizawa is the unspoken source of his Class C access.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Does not appear in person on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v6-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: named as the shared enemy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
